Subject: [PATCH] The boxes laid out across the wider screen (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

From a reference drawn for the wider screen (2026-10-16): the panel of
the Pokémon looked at (its sprite in 3D, its text, its types) at the
screen's left edge; the box (its wallpaper sliding past as the boxes
change, the party's tray, the icons, the hand, the buttons) at the right
edge; the wallpaper's edge between them. The boxes to jump to and an
item's description, put across the screen, stay in the middle with
their sprites. The message box and the menus, whose frames the boxes
draw themselves, are told to the port: the message box widens across the
screen like the game's other text boxes, the menus go to the right edge
with the box.
